Northbridge cuts its outlook on export controls

Northbridge Semiconductor cut its full-year revenue outlook to $4.1 billion=
 on
Wednesday, down from $4.6 billion, citing new export controls on advanced
packaging equipment.

The company said the controls will reduce shipments to two of its largest
customers. Shares fell 12% in after-hours trading.

Finance chief Priya Nadar told analysts the company still expects to be
free-cash-flow positive for the year.

